## Verification rules

Stay read-only. Compare the spec and backup. Read the integration brief and its source files.
Check decisions against the brief and binding wording. Check new edits for contradictions elsewhere in the spec.
For later passes, mark earlier must-fix IDs resolved or open with evidence. Check only those IDs and new edits.
Write the report to the lead through the runtime. The lead saves it as `<work>/verification-<round>.md`.

## Required report

- Decisions: <each decision ID: applied as decided or gap, with spec location and source evidence>
- Must fix: <each stable ID: spec location, defect, input or state → wrong result, and why it blocks implementation; or none>
- Notes: <claims without a failure scenario and other nonblocking observations; or none>
- Unverified: <pending user confirmations, unavailable checks and other limits; or none>
- Verdict: <ready to implement, or not ready to implement; readiness needs no must-fix items or unapplied decisions>

A must-fix claim without a failure scenario is a note. Notes do not trigger fixes.
The lead records your model from runtime evidence alongside this report.
